<h2><strong>Boss&rsquo;s Day Facts</strong></h2>
<ul>
<li>The word \'boss\' originated from the Dutch word \'baas\'. Baas means \'master\' which was the common title for the ship captain.</li>
<li>Other meanings for the word boss include: swelling, top-class, or cow/calf.</li>
<li>The first time the word \'boss\' was used as an American English term it was to replace the word \'master\', in 1625.</li>
